1
00:00:36,599 --> 00:00:39,978
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

2
00:00:40,103 --> 00:00:41,229
CONCEPDEUL

3
00:00:48,736 --> 00:00:51,406
The competition for new brands
is quite fierce, Director.

4
00:00:51,489 --> 00:00:55,702
This month alone, we've received samples
from over thirty brands.

5
00:00:55,785 --> 00:00:58,371
I see a lot of knockoffs
from the last Paris Fashion Week.

6
00:00:58,454 --> 00:01:01,541
Well, there were a lot of
groundbreaking designs.

7
00:01:01,624 --> 00:01:03,334
I think the domestic brands
were heavily influenced.

8
00:01:03,418 --> 00:01:08,882
Brands that only know how to copy
have no place at APPELLO.

9
00:01:08,965 --> 00:01:11,050
Let's just review these.

10
00:01:11,134 --> 00:01:13,636
Okay then, Hye-soo. I'll leave it to you.

11
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:15,722
I'll join you as soon as
I'm finished with the display.

12
00:01:15,805 --> 00:01:18,558
Okay, I'll start prepping the models
for the fitting right away.

13
00:01:18,641 --> 00:01:21,561
- Okay, let me know when you're ready.
- Okay.

14
00:01:24,063 --> 00:01:25,732
That's just like you.

15
00:01:25,815 --> 00:01:27,775
Not predictable...

16
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:30,445
You have your own distinct identity.

17
00:01:30,528 --> 00:01:32,280
That's how APPELLO started too.

18
00:01:32,363 --> 00:01:34,449
I started by collecting
what I wanted to wear,

19
00:01:34,532 --> 00:01:35,867
and it became a tiny curated shop.

20
00:01:36,743 --> 00:01:40,163
Now it's a platform
with hundreds of brands.

21
00:01:40,246 --> 00:01:41,247
The weight is much greater.

22
00:01:42,207 --> 00:01:45,293
You're bearing the weight.
I'm just providing the direction.

23
00:01:45,376 --> 00:01:46,836
If you veer too far off course,

24
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:48,504
you'll make everyone following you
stumble.

25
00:01:48,588 --> 00:01:53,218
I know,
that it's time to move forward together.

26
00:01:56,137 --> 00:01:57,055
Yes.

27
00:01:58,473 --> 00:02:01,601
Yes, CEO. As you wish,
I'll aim for mass appeal too.

28
00:02:06,397 --> 00:02:08,316
EPISODE 2

29
00:02:12,153 --> 00:02:14,280
The clothes on the man, his bracelet...

30
00:02:14,364 --> 00:02:16,533
- Make a note of that.
- Okay.

31
00:02:18,409 --> 00:02:21,120
And get a tie in a shade
as bright as this.

32
00:02:21,204 --> 00:02:23,706
Yes, got it.

33
00:02:23,790 --> 00:02:24,832
All right, great work, everyone.

34
00:02:24,916 --> 00:02:26,334
- Okay.
- Thank you.

35
00:02:26,417 --> 00:02:30,296
- Send me the photos from today's shoot.
- Okay. You can go, Director.

36
00:02:30,380 --> 00:02:31,839
Okay.

37
00:02:52,735 --> 00:02:56,781
D.N.X! D.N.X! We love you, D.N.X!

38
00:03:16,801 --> 00:03:18,887
You dropped this.

39
00:03:27,812 --> 00:03:29,814
Thank you.

40
00:03:34,110 --> 00:03:35,737
Aren't you getting in?

41
00:03:36,696 --> 00:03:37,697
Huh?

42
00:03:40,533 --> 00:03:41,784
Get in.

43
00:03:56,799 --> 00:03:59,177
Don't be nervous, Nam Da-reum.

44
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:01,221
Act as natural as possible.

45
00:04:08,186 --> 00:04:09,270
NAM DA-REUM

46
00:04:10,271 --> 00:04:14,484
- You're one of the new employees, right?
- Huh?

47
00:04:17,362 --> 00:04:18,988
Yes.

48
00:04:19,072 --> 00:04:20,865
Why weren't you at the welcome dinner?

49
00:04:23,701 --> 00:04:27,956
I was a little drunk,
so I left early yesterday.

50
00:04:29,165 --> 00:04:31,501
I see.

51
00:04:32,502 --> 00:04:34,879
Anyway, it's nice to meet you, Da-reum.

52
00:04:39,467 --> 00:04:40,927
How do you know my name?

53
00:04:42,178 --> 00:04:43,846
Let's work well together.

54
00:04:58,194 --> 00:04:59,612
I'll do my best.

55
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:04,784
See you around.

56
00:05:04,868 --> 00:05:07,370
Yes, Director.

57
00:05:14,711 --> 00:05:15,962
Goodbye.

58
00:05:36,608 --> 00:05:38,568
Oh my gosh.

59
00:05:39,736 --> 00:05:41,446
Oh my gosh!

60
00:05:41,529 --> 00:05:44,908
I even shook his hand!

61
00:05:46,659 --> 00:05:48,578
This is crazy!

62
00:05:51,831 --> 00:05:55,418
You played it cool. Good job.
Way to go, Nam Da-reum.

63
00:06:09,349 --> 00:06:10,808
Goodbye.

64
00:06:19,484 --> 00:06:22,946
WOLHAEUNBANG

65
00:06:35,458 --> 00:06:39,712
Hey.
What have you been doing here for days?

66
00:06:40,463 --> 00:06:42,131
You planning on switching careers?

67
00:06:42,215 --> 00:06:43,424
Should I?

68
00:06:45,218 --> 00:06:48,805
DNX has disbanded. Not many people would
remember Lee Chan anyway.

69
00:06:50,473 --> 00:06:52,058
Hey.

70
00:06:52,141 --> 00:06:53,101
Didn't I do a pretty good job?

71
00:06:53,977 --> 00:06:56,396
You should just open your own workshop.

72
00:06:59,482 --> 00:07:02,819
Hey, clean all this up
by the time I get back.

73
00:07:02,902 --> 00:07:04,445
Got it?

74
00:07:04,529 --> 00:07:05,572
Got it?

75
00:07:32,432 --> 00:07:34,434
- Hello.
- Hi there.

76
00:07:34,517 --> 00:07:36,561
Excuse me, how much is this?

77
00:07:36,644 --> 00:07:40,607
This is an experience workshop,
so we do not sell the items.

78
00:07:40,690 --> 00:07:43,067
A customer made this one themselves.

79
00:07:43,151 --> 00:07:47,071
There is a celebrity
I really, really love,

80
00:07:47,155 --> 00:07:49,449
and this is the design he uses
for his autograph.

81
00:07:50,617 --> 00:07:52,076
Today is my birthday,

82
00:07:52,160 --> 00:07:53,828
and I wanted to give it to myself
as a present.

83
00:07:54,787 --> 00:07:55,872
Can I really not buy it?

84
00:07:56,956 --> 00:08:01,419
I am sorry.
How about trying to make one yourself?

85
00:08:02,795 --> 00:08:05,506
I do not think I could make it
exactly like this.

86
00:08:05,590 --> 00:08:09,636
It is not as difficult as you might think.

87
00:08:11,638 --> 00:08:14,349
No, that is okay. Yes, I understand.

88
00:08:15,058 --> 00:08:16,893
- Thank you.
- Of course.

89
00:08:16,976 --> 00:08:19,270
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

90
00:08:42,168 --> 00:08:43,336
So that was you.

91
00:08:48,216 --> 00:08:50,927
- Good work today.
- Thanks! You too!

92
00:08:51,970 --> 00:08:55,682
You all worked so hard today.
I will see you tomorrow, okay?

93
00:08:55,765 --> 00:08:58,017
See you tomorrow. Bye!
See you all tomorrow! Get home safe!

94
00:08:59,894 --> 00:09:03,982
Da-reum seems to be
in a particularly good mood today.

95
00:09:04,065 --> 00:09:07,068
I know. And with how busy our team
has been lately...

96
00:09:07,151 --> 00:09:08,653
Min-a.

97
00:09:08,736 --> 00:09:12,031
If you are free, would you like to
grab a quick beer before heading home?

98
00:09:12,115 --> 00:09:14,075
Beer!

99
00:09:15,159 --> 00:09:16,703
No.

100
00:09:18,496 --> 00:09:19,497
"No"?

101
00:09:20,832 --> 00:09:22,375
SEONGJU STATION

102
00:09:25,837 --> 00:09:27,213
You are one of the new employees, right?

103
00:09:39,642 --> 00:09:40,643
Nice to meet you, Da-reum.

104
00:09:42,729 --> 00:09:45,481
It was nice to meet you.

105
00:09:51,321 --> 00:09:52,322
Let's see each other again.

106
00:10:05,460 --> 00:10:09,047
Let's see each other again!
Chan, let's see each other again!

107
00:10:09,797 --> 00:10:11,090
Da-reum, see you again!

108
00:10:12,592 --> 00:10:13,843
Bye!

109
00:10:18,431 --> 00:10:19,307
You are that happy, huh?

110
00:10:21,142 --> 00:10:22,685
Yeah.

111
00:10:22,769 --> 00:10:24,229
Anyone would think you won the lottery.

112
00:10:24,312 --> 00:10:28,024
She totally hit the jackpot.
I mean, for fans like us from out of town,

113
00:10:28,107 --> 00:10:29,234
we cannot even go to his workshop.

114
00:10:29,317 --> 00:10:32,237
And even at concerts,
you can barely see his face

115
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:34,113
because he looks so tiny.

116
00:10:34,197 --> 00:10:36,866
You have really made it, Namda.

117
00:10:36,950 --> 00:10:39,410
What can I say?
Do you want to take a sniff?

118
00:10:39,494 --> 00:10:40,703
Oh, come on!

119
00:10:41,412 --> 00:10:43,331
- No, no, no!
- Me too, me too!

120
00:10:43,414 --> 00:10:46,876
No! It will get worn out!
It is too precious!

121
00:10:48,670 --> 00:10:50,797
The day I first saw him in person...

122
00:10:52,131 --> 00:10:54,634
I will celebrate this day every year.

123
00:10:54,717 --> 00:10:57,554
Didn't you use to insist
Chan gave you that necklace?

124
00:10:57,637 --> 00:11:00,932
So you are finally admitting
it was just wishful thinking?

125
00:11:05,520 --> 00:11:09,858
But there is no way anyone but Chan
could have made this.

126
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:23,204
Excuse me.

127
00:11:28,042 --> 00:11:30,086
Happy birthday.

128
00:12:04,078 --> 00:12:06,748
But his voice back then
sounded just like Chan's.

129
00:12:06,831 --> 00:12:10,084
Hey, that is just your fangirl heart
coloring your memory.

130
00:12:11,711 --> 00:12:12,879
You think so?

131
00:12:12,962 --> 00:12:18,134
Anyway! I finally found met him.
What do I do now?

132
00:12:18,218 --> 00:12:19,844
Hey, I am not dreaming, am I?

133
00:12:21,596 --> 00:12:24,307
- Ow! That hurts! It hurts!
- You are not dreaming.

134
00:12:24,474 --> 00:12:26,100
APPELLO

135
00:12:28,478 --> 00:12:30,480
This year's Overseas Training
for Outstanding Employees

136
00:12:30,563 --> 00:12:32,565
is apparently for New York Fashion Week.

137
00:12:32,649 --> 00:12:33,942
New York?

138
00:12:34,025 --> 00:12:35,652
Perfect.

139
00:12:35,735 --> 00:12:37,278
So much to see,

140
00:12:38,488 --> 00:12:40,698
and so much work to do.

141
00:12:40,782 --> 00:12:42,617
Overseas Training
for Outstanding Employees?

142
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:45,995
- What's that?
- It's sort of a tradition here at APPELLO

143
00:12:46,079 --> 00:12:48,998
that Director Chan started
when the company was founded.

144
00:12:49,082 --> 00:12:50,792
Once a year, they pick
an Outstanding Employee

145
00:12:50,875 --> 00:12:52,252
to go on an overseas project.

146
00:12:52,335 --> 00:12:55,713
The selection will probably be made
around the first half of next year.

147
00:12:55,797 --> 00:13:00,176
Oh, thank you. Oh, Min-a.

148
00:13:00,260 --> 00:13:05,473
- So, does Director Chan go with them?
- Of course.

149
00:13:05,557 --> 00:13:07,725
He's never missed one.

150
00:13:07,809 --> 00:13:11,187
- Who picks the Outstanding Employee?
- The CEO.

151
00:13:13,982 --> 00:13:14,858
The CEO?

152
00:13:26,870 --> 00:13:28,079
AVOIDING THE CEO

153
00:13:33,793 --> 00:13:35,628
OVERSEAS TRAINING FOR OUTSTANDING
EMPLOYEES! BE SEEN!

154
00:13:39,257 --> 00:13:40,091
But...

155
00:13:41,217 --> 00:13:44,596
Can my goal really do a complete 180
like this?

156
00:13:46,014 --> 00:13:50,476
No. Nam Da-reum, you can do this.

157
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:51,561
Yes!

158
00:13:53,396 --> 00:13:54,272
First,

159
00:13:55,773 --> 00:13:59,277
I should find out
what kind of person the CEO is.

160
00:14:03,114 --> 00:14:06,159
- Here, have this while you work.
- Thank you.

161
00:14:08,369 --> 00:14:10,121
- By the way, ma'am...
- Yes?

162
00:14:10,205 --> 00:14:12,832
What does the CEO like?

163
00:14:13,625 --> 00:14:14,626
Why the sudden interest?

164
00:14:16,711 --> 00:14:20,632
I've shown a bad side of myself
since the first day of work.

165
00:14:20,715 --> 00:14:24,677
I guess I want to improve my image
and show I can work hard.

166
00:14:25,678 --> 00:14:26,679
Oh, really?

167
00:14:27,347 --> 00:14:30,183
The CEO... Hmm...

168
00:14:30,266 --> 00:14:34,979
Our CEO,
the capsule machine in the break room...

169
00:14:37,941 --> 00:14:38,942
The brown one?

170
00:14:39,901 --> 00:14:42,946
Chocolate latte.
Believe it or not, he has a sweet tooth.

171
00:14:44,155 --> 00:14:45,823
HOW TO WIN OVER CEO KANG HAGI,
CHOCOLATE LATTE

172
00:14:52,956 --> 00:14:56,334
Sir, would you like
a sweet chocolate latte?

173
00:14:56,417 --> 00:14:58,211
I just made a fresh cup.

174
00:15:01,214 --> 00:15:03,883
No, thank you. It raises my blood sugar,
so I only have one cup a day.

175
00:15:03,967 --> 00:15:06,553
I've already had one, so you can have it.

176
00:15:11,558 --> 00:15:12,559
Okay.

177
00:15:12,809 --> 00:15:14,644
HOW TO WIN OVER CEO KANG HAGI,
CHOCOLATE LATTE

178
00:15:16,271 --> 00:15:19,941
He usually spends some time on the rooftop
after lunch.

179
00:15:20,024 --> 00:15:22,569
He says he likes to get about 20 minutes
of sunlight a day.

180
00:15:22,861 --> 00:15:24,153
WINNING CEO HAGI, PHOTOSYNTHESIS BUDDY

181
00:15:31,911 --> 00:15:35,874
Oh. The CEO comes here too.

182
00:15:35,957 --> 00:15:38,793
- The view is amazing, isn't it?
- Yes, it is.

183
00:15:39,961 --> 00:15:44,257
I come up here after lunch
to get some sun, too.

184
00:15:45,008 --> 00:15:47,552
People need sunlight to stay healthy.

185
00:15:47,635 --> 00:15:49,846
Sir, did you know that
most people these days

186
00:15:49,929 --> 00:15:51,514
are vitamin D deficient?

187
00:15:51,598 --> 00:15:53,933
- Nam Da-reum.
- Yes?

188
00:15:56,769 --> 00:15:58,938
Huh?

189
00:15:59,022 --> 00:16:01,900
You're being distracting.
Please stop blocking the view.

190
00:16:04,152 --> 00:16:06,571
Okay. I'm sorry.

191
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:10,992
HOW TO WIN OVER CEO KANG HAGI,
PHOTOSYNTHESIS BUDDY

192
00:16:12,202 --> 00:16:16,581
And if you compliment the CEO's style,
he'll secretly like it.

193
00:16:16,706 --> 00:16:18,166
WINNING CEO HAGI, SO PRETTY, OUR HAGI

194
00:16:19,292 --> 00:16:21,211
Oh, sir!

195
00:16:21,294 --> 00:16:25,548
That shirt and tie combination
looks amazing on you.

196
00:16:25,632 --> 00:16:27,050
You could walk a runway.

197
00:16:27,133 --> 00:16:29,135
I pulled an all-nighter
in yesterday's clothes.

198
00:16:33,973 --> 00:16:34,849
Goodbye.

199
00:16:39,687 --> 00:16:42,106
Nothing is working out.

200
00:16:51,866 --> 00:16:55,119
"That shirt and tie combination
looks amazing on you.

201
00:16:55,203 --> 00:16:56,955
You look like you could walk a runway."

202
00:17:04,462 --> 00:17:05,463
You startled me.

203
00:17:11,886 --> 00:17:12,845
I looked into it, and it seems Nam Da-reum

204
00:17:12,929 --> 00:17:15,807
was recently working
at SE Corporation, and then--

205
00:17:15,890 --> 00:17:18,059
Just speak up.
It's just the two of us here.

206
00:17:18,142 --> 00:17:19,561
Yes, sir.

207
00:17:19,644 --> 00:17:23,022
Nam Da-reum was working at SE Corporation
and recently resigned.

208
00:17:24,899 --> 00:17:28,319
Actually, I get the feeling
she's approaching me for a reason.

209
00:17:28,403 --> 00:17:31,739
Could it be a honey trap
from Director Kim?

210
00:17:33,825 --> 00:17:34,701
Honey?

211
00:17:35,910 --> 00:17:38,288
- I don't think that's right.
- Exactly. That doesn't make any sense.

212
00:17:39,372 --> 00:17:42,083
Then maybe a cuteness ploy?
Trying to win you over with charm?

213
00:17:45,712 --> 00:17:46,921
That makes no sense either.

214
00:17:47,005 --> 00:17:48,715
Then is she just here to cause trouble?

215
00:17:59,225 --> 00:18:00,143
The CEO...

216
00:18:00,894 --> 00:18:02,228
How am I supposed to win him over?

217
00:18:02,312 --> 00:18:03,187
Why?

218
00:18:03,271 --> 00:18:08,109
I mean, whenever I try to talk to him,
he just says, "That's enough."

219
00:18:08,193 --> 00:18:13,323
There's no way in. He's impenetrable.
I'm not doing this because I like him.

220
00:18:13,406 --> 00:18:14,657
I'm trying to be the Outstanding Employee.

221
00:18:14,741 --> 00:18:17,368
Maybe he thinks you're hitting on him.

222
00:18:17,452 --> 00:18:20,121
It's not that he's impenetrable.
He has no intention of letting anyone in.

223
00:18:20,205 --> 00:18:22,624
Is that really why he's so guarded?

224
00:18:22,707 --> 00:18:24,584
No, no, no. He's like that with everyone.

225
00:18:24,667 --> 00:18:28,671
It's so bad the other employees
have a nickname for him.

226
00:18:28,755 --> 00:18:31,841
- They say he's like an icy wind.
- Hey, hey, hey, hey.

227
00:18:31,925 --> 00:18:33,384
Look at this.

228
00:18:33,468 --> 00:18:35,345
Exclusive Info: Rumors that A,
a famous idol-turned-top actor, is gay.

229
00:18:35,428 --> 00:18:37,472
His partner, B, is the CEO
of a fashion startup.

230
00:18:37,555 --> 00:18:39,682
Rumor is A hired B
to keep their relationship a secret.

231
00:18:39,766 --> 00:18:41,309
Whoa, isn't this obviously about APPELLO?

232
00:18:41,392 --> 00:18:44,187
It's definitely APPELLO.
Wow, Lee Chan is gay!

233
00:18:44,270 --> 00:18:45,230
He's gay...

234
00:18:47,315 --> 00:18:52,946
Hey, are A and B supposed to be
Chan and your CEO?

235
00:18:53,029 --> 00:18:54,113
What?

236
00:18:54,864 --> 00:18:56,574
Are they dating?

237
00:18:56,658 --> 00:18:59,619
What? That's ridiculous. Chan...

238
00:19:01,412 --> 00:19:02,830
He's straight.

239
00:19:02,914 --> 00:19:04,958
He said in an interview
that his first love

240
00:19:05,041 --> 00:19:06,501
was an older girl from his high school.

241
00:19:07,544 --> 00:19:10,838
- Then what is this?
- What do you mean? It's a rumor tabloid.

242
00:19:11,548 --> 00:19:14,175
Our CEO and Chan?

243
00:19:14,259 --> 00:19:16,177
Does that even make sense? Huh?

244
00:19:21,641 --> 00:19:22,600
Yeah, no.

245
00:20:06,311 --> 00:20:08,104
Unbelievable...

246
00:20:16,196 --> 00:20:17,697
Hey, wake up. Time to eat.

247
00:20:32,420 --> 00:20:33,963
This is it.

248
00:20:34,047 --> 00:20:35,965
What? Aren't you going to eat?

249
00:20:36,841 --> 00:20:37,967
This is what I have for breakfast.

250
00:20:39,302 --> 00:20:40,720
Hey, the drinking was just an excuse.

251
00:20:40,803 --> 00:20:42,639
You came because you wanted
to eat this, didn't you?

252
00:20:43,806 --> 00:20:44,807
You got it.

253
00:20:49,270 --> 00:20:51,856
Yes, this is the flavor I remember.

254
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:53,816
Hey, this tastes just like
your mom used to make--

255
00:21:04,577 --> 00:21:07,372
Man, it feels so good
to have a home-cooked meal.

256
00:21:08,248 --> 00:21:10,875
- Can I stay at your place for a while?
- Hey, forget it.

257
00:21:10,959 --> 00:21:12,460
My back hurts from the couch
because of you.

258
00:21:12,544 --> 00:21:14,379
Why? We could've slept together.

259
00:21:15,630 --> 00:21:17,465
Are you crazy?

260
00:21:17,549 --> 00:21:19,884
I'm late. Eat, clean up, and then go.

261
00:21:21,094 --> 00:21:22,095
Hey, hey.

262
00:21:22,929 --> 00:21:25,223
Take this at least. You didn't even eat.

263
00:21:25,306 --> 00:21:27,725
- What is this?
- A coworker of mine gave it to me.

264
00:21:28,726 --> 00:21:30,812
It should be good.
She has excellent taste.

265
00:21:30,895 --> 00:21:31,771
Take it.

266
00:21:33,773 --> 00:21:35,775
- I'm leaving.
- Okay.

267
00:21:35,859 --> 00:21:36,693
Clean up before you go!

268
00:21:38,987 --> 00:21:39,988
CEO'S OFFICE

269
00:22:48,473 --> 00:22:49,974
Yes.

270
00:22:50,058 --> 00:22:53,478
- CEO, weekly marketing meeting's ready.
- Okay, I'm on my way.

271
00:22:53,561 --> 00:22:55,021
Okay.

272
00:23:14,582 --> 00:23:15,917
Damn it...

273
00:23:20,547 --> 00:23:22,882
Hey. Come get this right now.

274
00:23:22,966 --> 00:23:24,217
Yes,

275
00:23:24,300 --> 00:23:28,513
The gorpcore look is trending
for this lookbook shoot,

276
00:23:28,596 --> 00:23:31,975
so we're planning to use that
as our concept.

277
00:23:37,982 --> 00:23:44,737
So, lately the trending hobbies are
hiking, tennis, running, and so on,

278
00:23:44,821 --> 00:23:48,491
but they felt a bit too sporty...

279
00:23:48,575 --> 00:23:50,994
So, what's the bottom line?

280
00:23:52,745 --> 00:23:55,248
- Pardon?
- The point.

281
00:23:55,331 --> 00:23:56,666
The point...

282
00:23:59,627 --> 00:24:00,753
REASON FOR FINAL CONCEPT SELECTION

283
00:24:00,837 --> 00:24:05,133
The concept for next season's visual shoot

284
00:24:06,050 --> 00:24:07,302
is camping.

285
00:24:08,970 --> 00:24:09,804
Camping.

286
00:24:10,847 --> 00:24:13,224
I like it. From now on, with your reports,

287
00:24:14,350 --> 00:24:16,728
please keep them under one minute.

288
00:24:17,437 --> 00:24:20,940
The detail I'm looking for isn't
a long-winded explanation

289
00:24:21,024 --> 00:24:22,233
but the results of your work.

290
00:24:24,152 --> 00:24:25,695
Understood.

291
00:24:25,778 --> 00:24:27,030
So, is that everything?

292
00:24:27,113 --> 00:24:29,616
- Yes.
- This week, I want everyone

293
00:24:29,699 --> 00:24:31,951
to focus all their efforts
on the APPELLO fashion show.

294
00:24:32,035 --> 00:24:34,787
I'm thinking we could capture
the on-site atmosphere in advance

295
00:24:34,871 --> 00:24:38,124
to promote it on our channels.
Any volunteers?

296
00:24:41,961 --> 00:24:45,506
One last thing,
the CEO likes proactive people.

297
00:24:45,590 --> 00:24:48,092
The kind who are always willing
to step up.

298
00:24:48,176 --> 00:24:50,845
I'll do it.

299
00:24:52,347 --> 00:24:55,892
Since everyone else seems to be busy
with their work,

300
00:24:55,975 --> 00:24:57,393
I would like to do it.

301
00:24:57,477 --> 00:25:01,523
Yes, since Da-reum is supporting
APPELLO's social media management,

302
00:25:01,606 --> 00:25:04,317
I think she would be very helpful.

303
00:25:07,820 --> 00:25:09,155
All right, then.

304
00:25:10,365 --> 00:25:12,784
We're going to the rehearsal today,

305
00:25:12,867 --> 00:25:14,494
so be at the CEO's Office by two.

306
00:25:14,577 --> 00:25:16,037
Okay.

307
00:25:16,913 --> 00:25:18,081
Da-reum.

308
00:25:18,164 --> 00:25:22,085
This is your first time working on-site.
Will you be okay?

309
00:25:22,794 --> 00:25:24,796
CEO.

310
00:25:24,879 --> 00:25:28,174
I think it would be better
if I went instead.

311
00:25:28,258 --> 00:25:30,385
Let's give our volunteer a chance.

312
00:25:31,219 --> 00:25:33,054
- Yes, sir.
- That will be all.

313
00:25:33,137 --> 00:25:35,390
- Yes.
- Understood.

314
00:25:37,016 --> 00:25:38,268
You got this!

315
00:26:03,418 --> 00:26:04,377
CEO...

316
00:26:21,728 --> 00:26:22,937
Look at that razor-sharpness.

317
00:26:24,147 --> 00:26:25,857
Just like its owner.

318
00:26:28,026 --> 00:26:29,694
I can't believe
I squatted in a place like this.

319
00:26:41,831 --> 00:26:44,417
I want to be an Outstanding Employee
and go on that trip too.

320
00:26:53,551 --> 00:26:54,886
What's this?

321
00:26:55,553 --> 00:26:59,349
His eyes... What's with that look?

322
00:27:22,038 --> 00:27:26,167
How can I make my feelings reach you?

323
00:27:27,210 --> 00:27:29,295
I love you, Chan.

324
00:27:29,671 --> 00:27:33,007
- I Love you, Chan.
- I Love you, Chan?

325
00:27:39,389 --> 00:27:45,311
<i>Unable to say the words 'I love you,'</i>

326
00:27:45,395 --> 00:27:50,483
<i>because my heart is a foolish coward</i>

327
00:27:52,151 --> 00:27:57,657
<i>Unable to even wipe away your tears</i>

328
00:27:59,242 --> 00:28:00,535
<i>How can I make my feelings reach you?</i>

329
00:28:03,162 --> 00:28:04,330
<i>I love you.</i>

330
00:28:05,707 --> 00:28:06,541
HOW CAN I REACH YOU...?

331
00:28:06,624 --> 00:28:07,542
<i>Chan</i>

332
00:28:12,213 --> 00:28:14,257
<i>Is all I can do...</i>

333
00:28:15,425 --> 00:28:16,968
That... that rumor tabloid...

334
00:28:18,469 --> 00:28:19,804
It must be true.

335
00:28:22,515 --> 00:28:24,934
What do I do? What do I do?

336
00:28:36,529 --> 00:28:37,614
NO IMPORTANT DOCUMENTS ON DESK

337
00:28:37,697 --> 00:28:41,284
- Were you waiting long?
- What? No, I just got here.

338
00:28:41,367 --> 00:28:44,996
I've placed the report
from the Weekly Meeting here.

339
00:28:45,079 --> 00:28:46,664
CEO.

340
00:28:57,717 --> 00:28:58,760
NO SIGN OF A CONFIDENTIAL LEAK

341
00:29:05,266 --> 00:29:08,895
- Let's go.
- What? Oh, yes.

342
00:29:08,978 --> 00:29:09,979
Let's go.

343
00:29:24,577 --> 00:29:26,204
- These days...
- Yes?

344
00:29:28,790 --> 00:29:30,250
Is the job market really tough?

345
00:29:32,919 --> 00:29:36,089
Yes, I suppose so. That's just how it is.

346
00:29:37,465 --> 00:29:38,383
With a résumé like yours,

347
00:29:38,466 --> 00:29:40,218
I'd think you could get
into any major company.

348
00:29:40,301 --> 00:29:42,095
Oh, no, not at all.

349
00:29:42,178 --> 00:29:43,221
By any chance,

350
00:29:44,430 --> 00:29:46,391
is there a special reason
you came to APPELLO?

351
00:29:49,811 --> 00:29:53,022
Actually,
I wanted to get to know myself better.

352
00:29:53,106 --> 00:29:55,441
Instead of just padding my résumé,

353
00:29:55,525 --> 00:29:58,069
I wanted to find out
what I'm truly passionate about.

354
00:29:58,152 --> 00:30:01,531
So I followed my heart.

355
00:30:02,949 --> 00:30:03,908
And...

356
00:30:04,951 --> 00:30:08,121
there was also someone
I really wanted to meet.

357
00:30:10,707 --> 00:30:11,708
And who would that be?

358
00:30:13,501 --> 00:30:14,919
Huh?

359
00:30:16,796 --> 00:30:19,340
- Did I just say that out loud?
- You must have, because I heard you.

360
00:30:23,136 --> 00:30:26,431
Well, what I meant was...

361
00:30:27,181 --> 00:30:30,226
I wanted to meet people
from various fields while working?

362
00:30:30,310 --> 00:30:31,561
Something like that, yeah.

363
00:30:35,982 --> 00:30:39,402
CEO, can I ask you something too?

364
00:30:40,737 --> 00:30:41,988
Yes.

365
00:30:42,071 --> 00:30:45,575
CEO, why did you come to APPELLO?

366
00:30:49,537 --> 00:30:52,332
It started because of one person.

367
00:30:52,415 --> 00:30:53,833
Could it be...

368
00:30:54,792 --> 00:30:56,211
Chan?

369
00:30:56,294 --> 00:30:58,713
But now, APPELLO is my everything.

370
00:31:05,261 --> 00:31:06,387
APPELLO IN NAMSAN

371
00:31:20,818 --> 00:31:23,363
APPELLO IN NAMSAN

372
00:31:31,913 --> 00:31:33,665
- What's this? A lucky draw?
- Yes, it is.

373
00:31:33,748 --> 00:31:34,832
Keep up the good work.

374
00:31:38,836 --> 00:31:40,713
Like this?

375
00:31:42,423 --> 00:31:43,925
You're all working so hard.

376
00:31:52,517 --> 00:31:53,810
So cool.

377
00:31:55,478 --> 00:31:57,647
Is she putting on an innocent act,
or what?

378
00:31:58,982 --> 00:32:00,733
Oh, CEO!

379
00:32:01,401 --> 00:32:04,028
I can't believe you came
all the way out here yourself.

380
00:32:05,071 --> 00:32:06,865
- Hello.
- Of course. I had to come.

381
00:32:06,948 --> 00:32:09,492
- Are the preparations going well?
- Oh, yes. They're going great.

382
00:32:09,576 --> 00:32:11,995
A new brand like us
could never have dreamed

383
00:32:12,078 --> 00:32:13,037
of a fashion show like this.

384
00:32:13,121 --> 00:32:16,291
Thank you so much for giving us
this amazing opportunity.

385
00:32:16,374 --> 00:32:21,254
Not at all. Your brand is so appealing
that the opportunity came naturally.

386
00:32:21,337 --> 00:32:23,923
But I see some items
I haven't seen before.

387
00:32:24,007 --> 00:32:29,262
An event like this is a rare opportunity.

388
00:32:29,345 --> 00:32:33,850
We even took out a loan
to create a ton of new products.

389
00:32:33,933 --> 00:32:35,143
Well, if the inventory piles up,

390
00:32:35,226 --> 00:32:37,937
it'll be hard to survive till next season,
but...

391
00:32:38,021 --> 00:32:40,607
No, no! Knock on wood!

392
00:32:40,690 --> 00:32:44,027
Yes, I... I'll make it so
when people see our clothes,

393
00:32:44,110 --> 00:32:46,070
they'll think, "Oh, that's go.co!"

394
00:32:46,154 --> 00:32:48,990
I'll make it so they can recognize it
and love it. That's what I'll do.

395
00:32:49,073 --> 00:32:51,075
Yes, I'm confident!

396
00:32:51,159 --> 00:32:53,203
- All right, then. Good luck.
- Yes.

397
00:32:53,286 --> 00:32:56,164
- I'll see you at the show.
- Got it. Good luck to you too, CEO! Yes.

398
00:32:56,247 --> 00:32:58,583
- Go get 'em!
- Go get 'em!

399
00:33:04,088 --> 00:33:05,340
Why do you keep smiling?

400
00:33:08,009 --> 00:33:13,973
It just occurred to me that
fashion brands and pop idols are similar.

401
00:33:14,057 --> 00:33:16,559
- Pop idols?
- Yes.

402
00:33:16,643 --> 00:33:21,397
They make their presence known on stage,
and their visuals make hearts pound,

403
00:33:21,481 --> 00:33:23,191
and most of all,
they're loved by their fans

404
00:33:23,274 --> 00:33:24,150
for a long, long time.

405
00:33:28,821 --> 00:33:33,576
I wonder how much effort everyone put in
just to get on that stage once.

406
00:33:35,828 --> 00:33:39,874
I really hope
this fashion show is a success.

407
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:43,253
I'll work really hard too.

408
00:34:00,478 --> 00:34:02,522
All right, the opening is starting!

409
00:34:03,147 --> 00:34:06,359
First model, enter on your spot!
Keep a three-second interval!

410
00:34:06,442 --> 00:34:09,028
Okay, go!

411
00:34:24,836 --> 00:34:26,921
So cool.

412
00:34:37,140 --> 00:34:38,099
- What's going on?
- Cut, cut, cut!

413
00:34:38,182 --> 00:34:39,684
- What happened?
- What? Are you okay?

414
00:34:39,767 --> 00:34:41,603
Hey, assistant director,
go check on the model.

415
00:34:41,686 --> 00:34:42,937
Yes, sir.

416
00:34:43,563 --> 00:34:45,648
Okay, let's reduce the amount of dry ice.

417
00:34:45,732 --> 00:34:49,986
- Did that happen because of the dry ice?
- Yes, that's likely the reason.

418
00:34:50,069 --> 00:34:52,113
If there's too much dry ice,
it creates water vapor and...

419
00:34:56,492 --> 00:34:59,954
So that's why he almost fell
on stage back then.

420
00:35:00,038 --> 00:35:02,999
Let's wipe down the stage
and have someone test walk on it.

421
00:35:03,082 --> 00:35:05,877
Is anyone on our staff wearing heels?

422
00:35:12,008 --> 00:35:14,135
Should I try?
The heels on these shoes are low,

423
00:35:14,219 --> 00:35:15,887
so I think it'll be okay.

424
00:35:15,970 --> 00:35:19,098
- Then could I ask you to do that?
- Of course.

425
00:35:19,182 --> 00:35:20,725
Why you, Nam Da-reum?

426
00:35:20,808 --> 00:35:22,602
Come on, if the models get hurt,
it'll disrupt the show.

427
00:35:22,685 --> 00:35:24,103
I'll go and walk slowly to test it out.

428
00:35:24,187 --> 00:35:27,190
- Should I go backstage?
- Yes, thank you.

429
00:35:53,591 --> 00:35:56,261
- Whoa! Whoa!
- Nam Da-reum!

430
00:36:21,452 --> 00:36:23,538
- A-are you okay?
- Yes.

431
00:36:24,289 --> 00:36:26,040
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

432
00:36:26,791 --> 00:36:29,127
You were just supposed to walk.
Why did you do a turn?

433
00:36:29,210 --> 00:36:32,839
I let my guard down
and almost cracked my head open. Yes.

434
00:36:33,923 --> 00:36:36,009
I know, right? What was I thinking?

435
00:36:37,510 --> 00:36:40,763
There's some moisture here at the front,
so...

436
00:36:40,847 --> 00:36:43,016
I think you just need to wipe down
the front here carefully.

437
00:36:43,099 --> 00:36:44,517
- Yes.
- Okay.

438
00:36:44,601 --> 00:36:47,020
- Hey, assistant director, go wipe it now.
- Then...

439
00:36:52,817 --> 00:36:56,237
Yes, they may seem perfect in every way,

440
00:36:56,321 --> 00:36:58,823
but they are clumsy and hurt
when it comes to love.

441
00:36:58,907 --> 00:37:00,241
Please welcome Lee Chan,
who plays Sung-joon,

442
00:37:00,325 --> 00:37:03,870
and Yoon Cho-yi, who plays Iseo,
a character who grows

443
00:37:03,953 --> 00:37:07,373
after experiencing the sweetest moments
and the most bitter breakup.

444
00:37:07,457 --> 00:37:10,084
The two stars of "Bittersweet,"
please make a heart.

445
00:37:12,587 --> 00:37:14,005
Please look to your left.

446
00:37:14,088 --> 00:37:15,590
To the center,

447
00:37:15,673 --> 00:37:17,133
and to your right.

448
00:37:18,092 --> 00:37:19,177
That's great.

449
00:37:20,470 --> 00:37:22,263
It's now time for the press conference.

450
00:37:22,347 --> 00:37:24,390
Reporters with questions,
please raise your hand,

451
00:37:24,474 --> 00:37:25,892
and we'll bring you a microphone.

452
00:37:26,809 --> 00:37:27,644
Yes.

453
00:37:27,727 --> 00:37:30,730
Just from the trailer,
your chemistry seems truly exceptional.

454
00:37:30,813 --> 00:37:32,190
While working on this project,

455
00:37:32,273 --> 00:37:35,401
did you develop romantic feelings
for each other?

456
00:37:35,485 --> 00:37:39,572
Honestly, who wouldn't get flustered
looking at Lee Chan?

457
00:37:39,656 --> 00:37:42,492
Maybe it's because I've personally been
a long-time fan,

458
00:37:43,243 --> 00:37:45,954
but I think it definitely helped
with my emotional scenes.

459
00:37:47,789 --> 00:37:50,166
Cho-yi is so lovely, isn't she?

460
00:37:50,250 --> 00:37:54,796
I feel that charm has blended
into our drama very well.

461
00:37:54,879 --> 00:37:58,841
If I were to meet someone like Iseo
in real life,

462
00:37:59,968 --> 00:38:01,803
I'd have no choice but
to fall in love, right?

463
00:38:05,890 --> 00:38:08,643
LEE CHAN AND YOON CHO-YI:
DID SPARKS REALLY FLY WHILE FILMING?

464
00:38:10,270 --> 00:38:12,397
- Ah, you all worked hard today.
- You worked hard.

465
00:38:12,480 --> 00:38:13,565
You worked hard.

466
00:38:13,648 --> 00:38:15,233
- I'll get going.
- Okay, take care.

467
00:38:15,316 --> 00:38:16,234
You worked hard, Director.

468
00:38:19,988 --> 00:38:21,573
You worked hard.

469
00:38:21,656 --> 00:38:23,658
Yes, you too.

470
00:38:29,873 --> 00:38:30,874
Hold on a second.

471
00:38:38,047 --> 00:38:40,592
Did you get the gift I gave you?

472
00:38:41,301 --> 00:38:42,677
I gave it to a friend.

473
00:38:42,760 --> 00:38:44,095
What?

474
00:38:46,306 --> 00:38:48,641
You're ignoring all my calls.
Are you going to keep doing this?

475
00:38:48,725 --> 00:38:50,143
Cho-yi,

476
00:38:51,853 --> 00:38:52,854
we broke up.

477
00:38:53,813 --> 00:38:55,899
- Just accept it.
- No.

478
00:38:56,733 --> 00:39:00,403
I can't break up with you. No, I won't.

479
00:39:01,070 --> 00:39:04,073
I was serious about us. Weren't you?

480
00:39:05,408 --> 00:39:06,409
Not even for a single moment?

481
00:39:06,492 --> 00:39:07,952
I had feelings for you.

482
00:39:08,953 --> 00:39:12,665
- But it wasn't love.
- But why?

483
00:39:13,750 --> 00:39:14,959
What's wrong with me?

484
00:39:17,921 --> 00:39:19,589
It's not you.

485
00:39:19,672 --> 00:39:21,424
We just weren't a good fit.

486
00:39:21,507 --> 00:39:22,967
Cho-yi,

487
00:39:24,302 --> 00:39:26,930
You're enough just the way you are.

488
00:39:27,013 --> 00:39:28,306
Okay?

489
00:39:32,518 --> 00:39:35,563
I tried so hard and endured so much
to make it work for you.

490
00:39:36,648 --> 00:39:37,857
You say we're not a good match?

491
00:39:37,941 --> 00:39:38,900
Is it really love

492
00:39:38,983 --> 00:39:40,485
when you have to try so hard
and just endure?

493
00:39:42,278 --> 00:39:44,489
Someone you can be yourself with,

494
00:39:45,990 --> 00:39:47,158
find someone like that.

495
00:39:49,994 --> 00:39:51,246
That's hilarious.

496
00:39:51,329 --> 00:39:53,414
Acting all polite and considerate.

497
00:39:54,624 --> 00:39:57,544
So you're just going to leave,
acting like you're the bigger person?

498
00:39:58,211 --> 00:39:59,128
I'm

499
00:40:00,421 --> 00:40:01,589
never breaking up with you.

500
00:40:03,049 --> 00:40:04,551
So,

501
00:40:05,718 --> 00:40:06,761
you'll have to deal with it too.

502
00:40:46,384 --> 00:40:47,302
Well...

503
00:40:48,094 --> 00:40:49,846
Should we listen to some music?

504
00:40:49,929 --> 00:40:51,890
Yes, I'd love that.

505
00:41:00,148 --> 00:41:01,608
Wait, what?

506
00:41:05,987 --> 00:41:06,821
INCOMING CALL: LEE CHAN

507
00:41:11,868 --> 00:41:14,787
- Hello.
- Where are you?

508
00:41:14,871 --> 00:41:18,416
- It's really him.
- I'm almost at the office. Where are you?

509
00:41:18,499 --> 00:41:20,585
Me? I don't know.

510
00:41:21,586 --> 00:41:24,047
Why? We spent all night together.
You miss me already?

511
00:41:24,923 --> 00:41:26,090
All night?

512
00:41:30,345 --> 00:41:32,513
Hey, stop messing around, okay?

513
00:41:32,597 --> 00:41:36,142
Why? The vibe was great
until this morning.

514
00:41:36,226 --> 00:41:39,145
- Until this morning?
- So what do you want me to get?

515
00:41:39,229 --> 00:41:41,731
Never mind. I'll just throw it away.
It's better you don't see it.

516
00:41:46,611 --> 00:41:50,323
How can I get my feelings across to you?

517
00:41:50,406 --> 00:41:51,574
I love you...

518
00:41:52,325 --> 00:41:53,243
Chan.

519
00:41:59,749 --> 00:42:02,585
Is he going to throw that card away?

520
00:42:05,713 --> 00:42:07,090
Powering off.

521
00:42:15,640 --> 00:42:16,641
DNX

522
00:42:17,976 --> 00:42:20,853
'DEAR MY LIGHT,' D.N.X

523
00:42:45,503 --> 00:42:46,504
The CEO

524
00:42:47,839 --> 00:42:49,424
was really in love with him.

525
00:42:54,304 --> 00:42:57,807
How did I end up finding out
a secret like this?

526
00:43:00,184 --> 00:43:01,728
You haven't gone home yet?

527
00:43:11,404 --> 00:43:15,658
<i>Dear my light
The one who shined so brightly on me</i>

528
00:43:15,742 --> 00:43:18,328
<i>the one who filled my dark nights</i>

529
00:43:18,411 --> 00:43:22,081
<i>I was so grateful you were by my side</i>

530
00:43:22,165 --> 00:43:26,085
<i>Now I'll become your starlight</i>

531
00:43:26,169 --> 00:43:28,504
<i>Spread endlessly before our eyes</i>

532
00:43:29,255 --> 00:43:32,675
<i>if we light up each other
under the night sky...</i>

533
00:43:32,759 --> 00:43:33,593
Director Chan...

534
00:43:33,676 --> 00:43:35,470
How have you been?

535
00:43:37,639 --> 00:43:38,890
Yes.

536
00:43:41,017 --> 00:43:42,894
Hello.

537
00:43:47,899 --> 00:43:50,902
Who was your bias in DNX?

538
00:43:53,154 --> 00:43:54,656
Huh?

539
00:43:56,074 --> 00:43:56,991
How did you know?

540
00:43:57,075 --> 00:43:59,285
You were listening to our song
from ten years ago.

541
00:44:06,876 --> 00:44:08,545
By any chance

542
00:44:11,881 --> 00:44:13,550
was it me?

543
00:44:23,643 --> 00:44:25,019
It was, right?

544
00:44:26,980 --> 00:44:27,814
I knew it.

545
00:44:29,065 --> 00:44:32,694
I'm so screwed... Oh, man.

546
00:44:32,777 --> 00:44:34,279
Um...

547
00:44:35,363 --> 00:44:39,576
- How did you guess everything all at once?
- Just

548
00:44:40,326 --> 00:44:41,703
a hunch.

549
00:44:44,497 --> 00:44:46,875
Wow, this is amazing.

550
00:44:48,418 --> 00:44:52,213
Looks like you've been our fan
since you were a little kid.

551
00:44:52,297 --> 00:44:54,048
Feel free to call me Chan
when we're alone.

552
00:44:54,132 --> 00:44:56,217
But still...

553
00:44:56,301 --> 00:44:57,635
And I'll

554
00:44:59,429 --> 00:45:01,347
call you Da-reum. Is that okay?

555
00:45:06,019 --> 00:45:07,020
Okay.

556
00:45:08,104 --> 00:45:09,105
Chan.

557
00:45:13,109 --> 00:45:16,112
It's been over ten years
since DNX disbanded.

558
00:45:16,196 --> 00:45:18,448
It's nice that
people still listen to our music.

559
00:45:18,531 --> 00:45:21,075
- Thank you.
- Oh, it's nothing.

560
00:45:22,285 --> 00:45:27,624
I've listened to it for so long,
it's just part of my routine.

561
00:45:27,707 --> 00:45:29,876
When I'm walking, when I'm working...

562
00:45:30,501 --> 00:45:33,046
I just find myself
listening to it naturally.

563
00:45:34,297 --> 00:45:36,090
NAM DA-REUM

564
00:45:40,887 --> 00:45:43,723
- Let me see your phone.
- What?

565
00:45:49,938 --> 00:45:53,358
I left mine at the office.

566
00:46:31,771 --> 00:46:32,772
There.

567
00:46:40,113 --> 00:46:41,614
Call me.

568
00:46:44,617 --> 00:46:46,035
Okay.

569
00:46:50,415 --> 00:46:51,791
You will, right?

570
00:46:54,669 --> 00:46:56,421
CAFÉ BENO

571
00:46:56,504 --> 00:46:58,047
No way!

572
00:46:59,382 --> 00:47:00,842
No way.

573
00:47:00,925 --> 00:47:03,094
Is this really Chan's number?

574
00:47:04,053 --> 00:47:04,888
Yes.

575
00:47:05,889 --> 00:47:07,473
Hey.

576
00:47:07,557 --> 00:47:09,017
Namda.

577
00:47:10,143 --> 00:47:12,937
- She's completely zoned out.
- A celebrity gave her his number.

578
00:47:13,646 --> 00:47:14,814
What could this mean?

579
00:47:14,898 --> 00:47:18,902
He told you to call, didn't he?
Call and you'll find out.

580
00:47:18,985 --> 00:47:22,113
Come on. He didn't really give it to me
expecting me to call, did he?

581
00:47:22,197 --> 00:47:24,324
It's just because I'm a coworker,

582
00:47:25,200 --> 00:47:28,036
- and a longtime fan...
- A longtime fan, so what?

583
00:47:30,121 --> 00:47:31,080
I don't know.

584
00:47:31,164 --> 00:47:35,376
Maybe he gave it to you
because he's actually interested in you.

585
00:47:35,460 --> 00:47:36,461
Yeah.

586
00:47:37,086 --> 00:47:40,715
He could have just saved his number
in her phone. Why go to the trouble?

587
00:47:40,798 --> 00:47:43,259
Why write it on her hand?
Isn't that totally flirting?

588
00:47:43,343 --> 00:47:47,180
Hey, no! That's definitely not it.

589
00:47:47,263 --> 00:47:48,848
Anyway

590
00:47:49,891 --> 00:47:51,476
we should at least save it.

591
00:47:52,602 --> 00:47:54,395
Just save it, got it?

592
00:47:59,025 --> 00:47:59,943
CALLING...

593
00:48:01,611 --> 00:48:03,571
What? Did you really call?

594
00:48:03,655 --> 00:48:09,536
Hey. Stop it, seriously.
Come here! Give it to me, quick! Hey!

595
00:48:11,955 --> 00:48:14,290
- What should I say?
- Just say hi.

596
00:48:18,294 --> 00:48:19,295
Hello?

597
00:48:23,758 --> 00:48:25,343
Chan...?

598
00:48:25,426 --> 00:48:26,636
Um

599
00:48:26,719 --> 00:48:28,012
this is Da-reum.

600
00:48:30,431 --> 00:48:31,683
Hello?

601
00:48:39,858 --> 00:48:42,193
Isn't this Director Lee Chan's number?

602
00:48:42,277 --> 00:48:43,528
The director?

603
00:48:44,904 --> 00:48:46,573
That's right.
This is Director Lee Chan's phone.

604
00:48:49,117 --> 00:48:51,494
Oh.

605
00:48:51,578 --> 00:48:55,039
I'm an employee at the director's company.

606
00:48:55,123 --> 00:48:57,834
Our Chani

607
00:48:58,501 --> 00:48:59,794
is taking a shower right now...

608
00:49:05,925 --> 00:49:06,926
I'm so sorry!

609
00:49:11,806 --> 00:49:15,143
A coworker? Yeah, right.
Calling him "Chan" like that.

610
00:49:15,226 --> 00:49:16,227
How ridiculous.

611
00:49:16,311 --> 00:49:17,270
DELETE 1 ITEM FROM CALL LOG?

612
00:49:23,484 --> 00:49:26,571
- What's the next scene?
- We're getting it ready...

613
00:49:33,077 --> 00:49:35,538
- What are you doing in my dressing room?
- The next scene.

614
00:49:36,331 --> 00:49:37,373
Run lines with me.

615
00:49:39,584 --> 00:49:41,419
- We have to work.
- Want some coffee?

616
00:49:41,502 --> 00:49:42,795
Coffee, coffee...

617
00:49:50,970 --> 00:49:51,846
Namda...

618
00:49:55,141 --> 00:49:56,809
- I told you not to! Look at this!
- Hey, calm down.

619
00:49:57,560 --> 00:49:59,687
I mean, he has a girlfriend.

620
00:49:59,771 --> 00:50:02,732
- Why is he leading her on like that?
- I told you it wasn't like that!

621
00:50:02,815 --> 00:50:05,151
You're just as bad!

622
00:50:06,319 --> 00:50:11,115
Why are you making such a scene?
I'm screwed.

623
00:50:11,199 --> 00:50:13,284
I'm so screwed.

624
00:50:13,368 --> 00:50:14,661
You too...

625
00:50:16,579 --> 00:50:19,249
- When did I tell you to call?
- You're the one who told me to.

626
00:50:20,458 --> 00:50:22,001
But...

627
00:50:24,003 --> 00:50:24,963
Actually, this is for the best.

628
00:50:25,713 --> 00:50:28,841
It would've been so awkward
if Chan had answered.

629
00:50:28,925 --> 00:50:30,051
Namda.

630
00:50:31,886 --> 00:50:33,304
Aren't you disappointed?

631
00:50:33,388 --> 00:50:37,267
Come on, Chan is only human.
He can have a girlfriend.

632
00:50:37,350 --> 00:50:42,355
Actually, I hope he dates and, you know?
I just want him to be happy.

633
00:50:45,692 --> 00:50:50,655
Wow, a true fan is on another level.

634
00:50:50,738 --> 00:50:52,407
I agree.

635
00:50:55,118 --> 00:50:56,077
What time is it?

636
00:50:56,160 --> 00:50:58,329
Hey, it's time for his show.

637
00:50:58,413 --> 00:50:59,873
It's the premiere, so let's watch
before you go.

638
00:51:18,433 --> 00:51:19,434
Hey.

639
00:51:21,686 --> 00:51:23,021
What's with that look on your face?

640
00:51:24,063 --> 00:51:28,026
Are you crazy? Who are you
to be disappointed?

641
00:51:28,776 --> 00:51:32,113
You've been a fan for 12 years.
A fan! Snap out of it!

642
00:51:43,166 --> 00:51:45,251
Did I just bother him
by calling for no reason?

643
00:51:46,502 --> 00:51:48,421
He'd better not think
I'm an obsessive fan.

644
00:51:50,632 --> 00:51:52,592
I don't know, I don't know.
I'm going to stop thinking about it.

645
00:52:07,565 --> 00:52:08,399
Wait a minute.

646
00:52:08,483 --> 00:52:11,152
I love you, Chan.

647
00:52:13,780 --> 00:52:15,448
If he has a girlfriend...

648
00:52:17,867 --> 00:52:18,868
Then what about the CEO?

649
00:52:22,455 --> 00:52:24,207
A real one-sided love?

650
00:52:28,628 --> 00:52:31,005
That's so sad for him too. So sad.

651
00:52:48,273 --> 00:52:49,357
SEONGJU

652
00:52:50,817 --> 00:52:52,694
SEONGJU

653
00:53:12,630 --> 00:53:14,007
One Americano is ready.

654
00:53:16,342 --> 00:53:17,760
Thank you.

655
00:53:39,574 --> 00:53:42,076
I wonder how long he's been in love
with him all by himself.

656
00:53:42,994 --> 00:53:46,247
Did he want to stay by his side,
even just as a friend?

657
00:54:05,934 --> 00:54:10,021
CEO. Here, drink this and cheer up.

658
00:54:11,064 --> 00:54:12,482
You got this!

659
00:54:25,203 --> 00:54:26,204
CEO!

660
00:54:27,205 --> 00:54:30,208
CEO, did you call for me?

661
00:54:31,501 --> 00:54:33,044
This has been up for too long.

662
00:54:33,127 --> 00:54:34,295
I'm so used to it, it's lost appeal.

663
00:54:34,379 --> 00:54:36,381
Right.

664
00:54:36,464 --> 00:54:38,091
I'll have this replaced
as soon as possible.

665
00:54:41,427 --> 00:54:44,639
I thought you didn't drink coffee.
What's this?

666
00:54:45,932 --> 00:54:47,183
Well...

667
00:54:47,267 --> 00:54:48,268
It's not bad.

668
00:54:51,896 --> 00:54:53,147
Good. One, two.

669
00:54:53,857 --> 00:54:57,193
Good. Look toward the window.
One, two. Good.

670
00:54:57,277 --> 00:54:58,403
Could you touch up his hair, please?

671
00:54:59,529 --> 00:55:02,448
Good. One, two. A slight smile. One, two.

672
00:55:02,532 --> 00:55:06,828
Good. One more time. One, two. Yes, great.

673
00:55:07,662 --> 00:55:11,291
- Photographer, you got some amazing shots.
- The tone is so good...

674
00:55:12,417 --> 00:55:14,711
- I'll go get the next set ready.
- Okay.

675
00:55:15,670 --> 00:55:19,048
- Hey, give me my phone.
- Here.

676
00:55:19,132 --> 00:55:21,676
- Did I miss any calls?
- Nope.

677
00:55:21,759 --> 00:55:23,511
Are you waiting for a call?

678
00:55:24,345 --> 00:55:25,597
No.

679
00:55:26,014 --> 00:55:26,973
UNREAD

680
00:55:27,056 --> 00:55:28,558
I was going to treat them to a meal...

681
00:55:31,060 --> 00:55:31,978
Who?

682
00:55:32,061 --> 00:55:33,354
Just someone.

683
00:55:34,856 --> 00:55:37,025
A friend I'm... grateful to.

684
00:55:39,611 --> 00:55:43,656
CEO, could you please confirm
the fashion show location?

685
00:55:43,740 --> 00:55:44,991
Yes.

686
00:55:50,496 --> 00:55:52,248
CEO, you drink coffee now?

687
00:55:53,875 --> 00:55:55,543
Yes.

688
00:55:56,211 --> 00:55:57,253
Well, I just sort of started...

689
00:55:57,962 --> 00:55:59,214
Go on.

690
00:55:59,297 --> 00:56:00,715
Okay.

691
00:56:00,798 --> 00:56:02,300
Um...

692
00:56:03,051 --> 00:56:04,344
Yes, CEO.

693
00:56:05,094 --> 00:56:08,139
What about Nam Da-reum?

694
00:56:08,223 --> 00:56:09,766
Her work, or anything else.

695
00:56:12,060 --> 00:56:14,938
From what I've seen, she's very diligent,

696
00:56:15,021 --> 00:56:17,690
and she's a go-getter
who always works hard.

697
00:56:18,566 --> 00:56:19,984
She's also a very cheerful person.

698
00:56:22,237 --> 00:56:24,280
She even asked me...

699
00:56:24,364 --> 00:56:26,783
how she could become
the Outstanding Employee.

700
00:56:26,866 --> 00:56:28,493
The Outstanding Employee?

701
00:56:28,576 --> 00:56:30,161
Yes.

702
00:56:41,673 --> 00:56:43,925
- Youngwoo, are the materials ready?
- Yes!

703
00:56:44,008 --> 00:56:46,010
- Wontae, let's go.
- Okay.

704
00:56:51,182 --> 00:56:52,308
Da-reum.

705
00:56:52,392 --> 00:56:54,394
Are the promotional messages
for the APPELLO fashion show

706
00:56:54,477 --> 00:56:57,397
- on KakaoTalk Friend all done?
- Yes.

707
00:56:57,480 --> 00:56:59,148
To remind them on the day
of the fashion show

708
00:56:59,232 --> 00:57:01,818
I made two versions. Just a moment.

709
00:57:12,871 --> 00:57:13,997
KAKAOTALK FRIEND

710
00:57:15,331 --> 00:57:16,291
NO SEARCH RESULTS

711
00:57:18,835 --> 00:57:21,045
- Why aren't you sending it?
- It's just...

712
00:57:23,381 --> 00:57:25,300
The file is gone.

713
00:57:26,885 --> 00:57:28,261
Gone?

714
00:57:28,344 --> 00:57:29,596
Yes.

715
00:57:32,390 --> 00:57:33,224
I'll redo it right away.

716
00:57:33,308 --> 00:57:35,476
Since I've already done it once,
it won't take long.

717
00:57:35,560 --> 00:57:38,605
You really did do it, right?

718
00:57:45,195 --> 00:57:46,446
The update is tomorrow,

719
00:57:46,529 --> 00:57:48,448
so you have to send it over
by the end of today.

720
00:57:50,366 --> 00:57:51,492
I'm sorry.

721
00:57:56,122 --> 00:57:57,540
Could it be...

722
00:57:57,624 --> 00:57:59,042
Did someone mess with it?

723
00:57:59,876 --> 00:58:02,086
No... that can't be it.

724
00:58:03,713 --> 00:58:04,923
I must have deleted it.

725
00:58:17,435 --> 00:58:19,270
APPELLO FASHION SHOW KAKAOTALK PROPOSAL,
BY: NAM DA-REUM

726
00:58:23,483 --> 00:58:25,193
Forget Outstanding Employee of the Year.

727
00:58:25,276 --> 00:58:27,695
It's hard enough just being
a regular employee.

728
00:58:36,663 --> 00:58:39,040
How does he work late every day?

729
00:58:41,668 --> 00:58:44,337
It's incredible.

730
00:58:56,683 --> 00:58:57,767
That's strange.

731
00:58:57,850 --> 00:59:01,354
I'm sure it was on my desktop.

732
00:59:04,190 --> 00:59:06,985
- Huh?
- Oh...

733
00:59:07,068 --> 00:59:09,028
I, I was just borrowing this.

734
00:59:09,112 --> 00:59:10,530
Yeah.

735
00:59:24,460 --> 00:59:25,587
No way.

736
00:59:25,670 --> 00:59:26,921
No way.

737
00:59:29,048 --> 00:59:30,049
I shouldn't jump to conclusions.

738
00:59:37,557 --> 00:59:38,683
JANGSINCHEON, GU DORIM BOARDING

739
01:00:37,200 --> 01:00:38,076
CEO.

740
01:00:38,159 --> 01:00:41,663
- You don't have an umbrella?
- CEO, what are you doing here?

741
01:00:41,746 --> 01:00:44,582
- I live in this neighborhood.
- Really? Me too.

742
01:00:45,333 --> 01:00:48,002
- Let's go. I'll walk you home.
- It's okay, you don't have to.

743
01:00:48,086 --> 01:00:49,420
You'd rather go by yourself?

744
01:00:49,504 --> 01:00:52,257
Huh? Oh, no!

745
01:01:01,933 --> 01:01:04,644
What happened to your car?
Why are you taking the subway, CEO?

746
01:01:05,395 --> 01:01:06,396
It's in for repairs.

747
01:01:08,648 --> 01:01:09,649
Did you work late today?

748
01:01:10,316 --> 01:01:11,985
Yes. A little.

749
01:01:14,070 --> 01:01:16,281
This late? That's more than a little.

750
01:01:18,241 --> 01:01:19,909
Do you have a lot of work to do?

751
01:01:19,993 --> 01:01:21,160
No.

752
01:01:22,078 --> 01:01:23,913
I made a few mistakes.

753
01:01:26,708 --> 01:01:31,045
You're so meticulous, CEO.
I bet you don't make mistakes, right?

754
01:01:31,129 --> 01:01:32,714
That's right, I don't.

755
01:01:35,717 --> 01:01:38,386
But I made a lot of them when I was new.

756
01:01:39,888 --> 01:01:41,931
Mistakes happen because you are working.

757
01:01:43,641 --> 01:01:47,020
If you don't do anything,
you won't make any mistakes.

758
01:01:48,313 --> 01:01:49,522
Don't be afraid. Just keep going.

759
01:01:50,899 --> 01:01:51,816
With your work

760
01:01:52,734 --> 01:01:54,194
and your mistakes.

761
01:01:57,280 --> 01:01:59,073
Thank you for saying that.

762
01:01:59,991 --> 01:02:01,659
I was getting all insecure for no reason.

763
01:02:03,536 --> 01:02:06,331
You're nicer than I expected, CEO.

764
01:02:07,749 --> 01:02:08,666
Than you expected?

765
01:02:08,750 --> 01:02:11,044
Yeah. Everyone avoids talking to you,

766
01:02:11,127 --> 01:02:12,937
afraid you'll shoot daggers
from your eyes.

767
01:02:13,168 --> 01:02:14,628
You didn't know?

768
01:02:19,552 --> 01:02:20,553
Hmph.

769
01:02:26,476 --> 01:02:28,228
Anyway, what a coincidence.

770
01:02:28,311 --> 01:02:29,979
I didn't know
you lived in the same neighborhood.

771
01:02:31,272 --> 01:02:32,607
Why haven't we run into each other?

772
01:02:39,739 --> 01:02:44,786
Bullying is the worst.
Do you even know how that feels?

773
01:02:46,871 --> 01:02:48,248
We might've run into each other.

774
01:02:49,832 --> 01:02:51,376
At a neighborhood bar.

775
01:02:52,168 --> 01:02:53,378
Huh?

776
01:02:54,003 --> 01:02:55,129
No way. If we had...

777
01:02:56,673 --> 01:02:57,757
it would've been at the library.

778
01:02:57,840 --> 01:03:02,887
My life is basically just
home, library, home, library.

779
01:03:03,846 --> 01:03:07,475
I can't believe there was a bar like this
in our neighborhood.

780
01:03:27,370 --> 01:03:28,621
That embarrassing past...

781
01:03:29,998 --> 01:03:32,000
Right, let's just bury it.

782
01:03:33,585 --> 01:03:34,419
CEO,

783
01:03:35,153 --> 01:03:36,170
that secret...

784
01:03:36,880 --> 01:03:38,423
I'll take it to my grave for you.

785
01:03:50,393 --> 01:03:53,730
CEO, my house is right over there.
It's late. You should get going.

786
01:03:53,813 --> 01:03:55,190
No, we're almost there. Why...

787
01:03:55,940 --> 01:03:56,816
Use it all the way to your door.

788
01:03:56,900 --> 01:04:00,361
Oh, thanks for walking me home!
You should get going now.

789
01:04:00,445 --> 01:04:01,905
Great work today!

790
01:04:04,157 --> 01:04:05,241
The roads are slippery.

791
01:04:05,325 --> 01:04:07,702
- If you let your guard down like that...
- CEO!

792
01:04:49,077 --> 01:04:52,914
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

793
01:05:03,883 --> 01:05:06,511
EPILOGUE

794
01:05:28,116 --> 01:05:31,077
APPELLO

795
01:06:16,581 --> 01:06:19,334
This is the last train for Gu Dorim.

796
01:06:19,417 --> 01:06:24,172
For passengers heading toward Songdam,
please board this train.

797
01:06:25,089 --> 01:06:26,966
SEONGJU

798
01:06:27,050 --> 01:06:29,010
THIS TRAIN: GU DORIM, NEXT: NONE,
APPROACHING GU DORIM

799
01:06:29,093 --> 01:06:31,387
GU DORIM

800
01:06:31,554 --> 01:06:33,139
INGUK

801
01:06:41,648 --> 01:06:42,774
She can't be here.

802
01:07:57,849 --> 01:08:00,518
What was that?

803
01:08:01,436 --> 01:08:02,562
Our stage!

804
01:08:02,645 --> 01:08:04,055
No!

805
01:08:04,080 --> 01:08:06,040
Everyone,
let's hang in there a bit longer!

806
01:08:06,123 --> 01:08:08,334
- Is she pretty?
- Come on.

807
01:08:08,359 --> 01:08:10,987
Maybe she was just too busy
to get in touch?

808
01:08:11,988 --> 01:08:14,866
Unless our information is being fed
to the SE in real time,

809
01:08:14,949 --> 01:08:15,783
it'd be hard to know.

810
01:08:15,867 --> 01:08:17,660
- Taxi! Taxi!
- CEO. Don't tell me...

811
01:08:17,744 --> 01:08:19,287
There really is a spy...

812
01:08:19,370 --> 01:08:20,955
Nam Da-reum.

813
01:08:21,873 --> 01:08:24,751
As of this moment, you're fired.

